Z||000004||DXR_DAD||02-27-2000||12:55 PM||||Gokart, Monkey is right, DXR  "Dimension X Racing" That is My sons (DXR_WILL) car club.<BR>All the info on the carbon fiber is on DaRkLoRD's site  <A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroproject.com</A> <P>Carolina, That is the stock tube, with a twist and a cut K&N at the mouth of the side scoop. Painted with plastic-kote rubber paint, the same stuff you dip your screwdrivers in or tool handles, and it holds up nice. It's been painted for a year and stilln looks good as the first day I did it.<P>It is a 86SE Paul did the sails using the GT style lettering, silver & red. And he did one hell of a job. Now I need to get it ready for that "BIG SHOW" in Modesto!!<P>Thanks guys!!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Carolina 88GT||02-27-2000||03:22 PM||||What size cone filter was that again?  About a 3 1/4" ? and did you remove the air canister all together, and what did you do with the MAT sensor?||||reg||1
Z||000006||DXR_DAD||02-27-2000||04:45 PM||||Carolina. I don't remember the patr# of the filter. It is about 6"long and 4 3/4 OD with a 3 1/4 adapter. The stock box is gone, then I cut the stock tube at an angle and rotated it from stock position until the cone was right at the scoop opening. I just guess the cut was at a 3 1/4 OD on the tube and it fit. The MAT was relocated to the end of the tube close to the cone end. on the back side so you can't see it. And yes you can hear the air sucked into it, sounds kinda good, I like the was it sounds at wide open   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> It runs fine after this mod, have had no probs.<p>[This message has been edited by DXR_DAD (edited 02-27-2000).]||||reg||1
